  "ui_receipt_limits": "Accessibility text files supplement the hash-bound operator observations above. The wrong-password text file contains only the unchanged-tree result; the invalid-password text and failed-open notification were visually observed by the authoring operator.",
  "container_interpretation": "All three complete variants are readable ZIP containers. No ZIP member has the encryption flag set. Both locked score.gpif members are readable as bytes but are not XML; editLocked/openLocked names distinguish these authored variants. This does not identify a cryptographic algorithm, key derivation, universal signature, or decryption API.",
  "decision": "Fixture-acquisition evidence delivered; awaiting fresh acceptance review. Import remains unsupported for both locked variants; no protected score reaches the public model or export. The malformed control is separate invalid data. Guitar Pro supplies mode-specific independent opening/unlocking evidence. A programmatic decryption implementation remains undefined because the member encoding and credential derivation are unknown. No decryption or password API is proposed and capability ratings remain missing.",
  "go_error_encoding": "Go XML errors can contain raw non-UTF-8 bytes from the protected member. go-results.json keeps the JSON-readable error_message and lossless error_message_hex; both are verified without changing the parser error."
